# The Quota slice: props that carry story (design/PITCHES.md 3c.1; engine: world/props.mjs). Gameplay
# engineer, 2026-10-22, from the eras table in PITCHES 3c; the era 2 texts are drafts for the story lead to
# rewrite in the slice's voice. Every prop tells about a person or an era (tells:). The five that persist
# across the eras carry a state for each of them; the slice plays era 2. tools/proplint.mjs checks them.
# In era 5 they stand where era 5's scenes are set (in:, world/props.mjs; story lead, 2026-10-23): the table in the
# antique shop's window, the last fair bowl on Mara's sill, the sign outside the archive on Exchange Street, the
# scale's bench on the square, the fence at the ring road's verge.
# Weighted-devices pass, era 2, 2026-10-23 (design/DEVICE-AUDIT.md; design/device-audit/era2.md): every prop is a
# thing the hands and the senses meet (carries:, touch:), never a page to read. The ration card is the relief
# token, the district ledger and the cell log are cut (the wedge under the scale's pan and Tomas's cap on the
# Brack kitchen nail carry what they carried), the district board is the brazier at the post.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the five that persist across the eras
@prop q.haldane_table
name: The Haldane table
place: q_haldane
mark: table
tells: household haldane
carries: touch
touch: press "Run your thumb over the goat on the leg" | Low on the leg, the carved goat with its head turned back. Your thumb finds it before your eyes do. Where the sanding stopped, the wood goes from smooth to rough under your nail.
state: 1 new | A new table in a barn, made out of a door. On one leg, low down, somebody has carved a Hesh goat with its head turned back.
state: 2 fewer ? bowls(haldane) <= 4 | The table Ilo made out of a barn door, with the hinge marks still in it. There are more stools than places laid, and nobody has moved the spare one back against the wall. Bet started sanding the goat off the leg in the autumn, when the crier started, and stopped halfway.
state: 2 laid | The table Ilo made out of a barn door, with the hinge marks still in it. Five places close together, on stools from three different houses. Bet started sanding the goat off the leg in the autumn, when the crier started, and stopped halfway.
state: 3 shifts | The door table, in a merchant's front room now, with ten families eating round it in shifts. The goat on the leg is black with hands.
state: 4 initials | The door table, its edge cut all round with children's initials. The oldest pair is near the hinge, and somebody has cut a line through them.
state: 5 shop | The door table, in the antique shop on the hill, with a price on a string round one leg. The goat is still on the leg, under the string.
in: 3 q3_mott_house
in: 4 q4_joss_flat
in: 5 q5_shop

@prop q.haldane_bowls
name: The bowls
place: q_haldane
mark: table
tells: household haldane
macro: 2.8 2.2
carries: touch
touch: lift "Lift the bowl off the shelf" ? era() == 2 & bowls(haldane) <= 4 | It's dry, and clean, and cold from the wall. Somebody has wiped it today. You put it back the way it was, turned over, and your hand doesn't want to let go of it. {sense: q.bowl.lift}
state: 1 five | Five bowls, matched, bought together at Osby fair with the wedding money.
state: 2 three ? bowls(haldane) <= 3 | Bowls on the shelf, turned over, beside the ones on the table. The ones on the shelf have been wiped. Somebody wipes them every day.
state: 2 four ? bowls(haldane) == 4 | One bowl on the shelf, turned over, just within reach of Bet's chair, so she can touch it without getting up.
state: 2 five | The bowls from Osby fair, all of them on the table, two chipped on the rim where the children hold them. A little gruel in each. You can see the glaze through it.
state: 3 relief | Odd bowls from the relief, no two the same. One has the relief's brand burnt into the bottom.
state: 4 plastic | Plastic bowls, red, from the market. The last fair bowl is on the windowsill with a plant in it.
state: 5 cleared ? has(e5.house_cleared) | One bowl from Osby fair on the windowsill, carried from flat to flat in a carrier bag since the clearance. The rest went in the bailiffs' crates.
state: 5 survivor | One bowl from Osby fair on Mara's windowsill, with a plant in it. Joss won't have it moved, not even to dust under it.
in: 3 q3_mott_house
in: 4 q4_joss_flat
in: 5 q5_mara_flat

@prop q.exchange_sign
name: The street sign
place: q_furrowe_door
mark: notice
tells: era
carries: sight
touch: press "Put a finger in the bullet hole" ? era() == 2 | The enamel's sharp round the hole, and the rust comes off on your fingertip, orange, like something that's been bleeding a long time.
state: 1 enamel | An enamel sign for Exchange Street, white on blue. The exchange put it up the year it opened, and polishes it.
state: 2 shot | The enamel street sign, white on blue, with two holes through the middle from October, when the militia fired over the bread queue. Rust has started running down from the holes like something leaking.
state: 3 renamed | The enamel sign is painted over with the new government's name for the street. The paint is already flaking off the old letters.
state: 4 defaced | Somebody has slapped white paint across the sign, the word they shout at the Chaffers, in letters a yard high. The council took two months to come and clean it, and did not finish.
state: 5 overpainted | The residents' group painted the sign over in heritage green. The old enamel shows through in the low sun.
in: 3 q3_square
in: 4 q4_exchange_street
in: 5 q5_archive

@prop q.exchange_scale
name: The exchange scale
place: q_tower
mark: scale
tells: era
carries: weight
touch: press "Put your hand under the sack pan" ? era() == 2 & !has(q.pencil_kept) | Under the sack pan, jammed hard between the pan and the frame, a flat wedge of iron the size of a hand. Your fingers come away cold, and the pan doesn't give at all. {sense: q.wedge.find, gives: q.lore.ledger}
state: 1 grain | The exchange's big scale, brass on an iron frame, for weighing grain at market. The weighman's stool is beside it.
state: 2 requisition | The exchange's big scale, weighing the requisition. A sack goes on, the arm drops on its stop and the roof rings, and two men carry the sack to the train. The weighman's stool is still beside it, and nobody sits on it.
state: 3 rations | The scale weighs rations now, a family's week at a time, with a queue round two sides of the square.
state: 4 base | The scale went for scrap. Its iron base is still bolted to the square, and children sit on it.
state: 5 bench | A council bench on the old scale's base, with a brass plate screwed to the back. Pigeons sit along the top of it in a row.
in: 3 q3_square
in: 4 q4_tower
in: 5 q5_square

@prop q.burial_fence
name: The burial ground
place: q_tower
mark: burial
tells: era
carries: touch
touch: hold "Hold the railing" ? era() == 2 | The iron is cold enough to hold on to your skin. Where the railings are bent apart for the gap, the paint has worn off to bright metal, from all the hands. {sense: cold.iron}
state: 1 iron | The burial ground on the hill's shoulder, behind iron railings. The church charges for the ground and the sexton's spade.
state: 2 dug ? prior(q.fact.cell_log) | The gap in the railings. The corner past it has been dug over since, for the fever rows, one long trench with lime on it and the ground gone yellow. Whatever was there first is under three others now. There's nothing to stand in front of.
state: 2 cart ? prior(world.dead.tomas) | The gap in the railings. The fever cart comes up from the town twice a day now, with a sheet over it, and the sexton has stopped charging for the spade. They're digging one long trench on the left and not filling it in between.
state: 2 corner ? q_class == inspector & q_figure == blamed & has(q.tomas_held) & cday() >= 45 | The gap in the railings. Past it, in the corner, a long patch of earth turned over and trodden flat, and no board. Will Brack said on the steps of the Crown that they put the hoarder in here on the Tuesday night. He said it to Ned as if it were good news.
state: 2 gap | A gap in the railings, bent apart, where people climb in at night to bury their own without paying the sexton for the spade. The new rows are on the left, where the ground was soft enough to dig in October.
state: 3 unmarked | A new section of the burial ground, unmarked, fenced with wire.
state: 4 overgrown | The famine section is overgrown to the waist. The railings have gone for scrap.
state: 5 moved | The fence has been moved back for the ring road. The corner it used to stand on is under the verge.
in: 3 q3_tower
in: 4 q4_tower
in: 5 q5_ring_verge

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- era 2, the slice's rooms
# The relief token (was the ration card; the id and the state id stay for the plates)
@prop q.haldane_ration_card
name: The relief token
place: q_haldane
mark: ration_card
tells: household haldane
macro: 2.2 2.6
carries: weight
touch: lift "Weigh the token in your hand" | It weighs nothing. A tin disc on a bootlace, worn bright at the edge where it's held up in the queue every morning. It's what they get the soup with. {sense: q.bowl.lift}
state: 2 card | The relief token on its nail by the door: a tin disc on a bootlace, punched with a hole for every mouth in the house. Somebody has scratched a little goat on the back with a nail, and then scratched across it, hard, till the goat's gone.

@prop q.district_map
name: The district map
place: q_returns
mark: map
tells: person q.ned
macro: 2.4 2.0
carries: sight
state: 2 worn | The district map on the wall, the eleven villages in Ned's own hand. It's been folded and unfolded so often that the crease runs right through Krall's End and the barns, and the paper's gone soft as cloth along it. There's a greasy patch over the hill where a thumb has rested.

@prop q.good_hat
name: Abel's good hat
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
mark: good_hat
tells: person q.abel
macro: 2.2 2.4
carries: weight
touch: lift "Take the hat down" ? era() == 2 | Heavier than a hat ought to be. The brass band is warm from the stove side of the peg. Inside, the leather's gone dark in a ring where Abel's head has been for forty years.
state: 2 hat | Abel's hat from the exchange, on its peg by the door. He polishes the brass band on Sundays with a bit of his own shirt. He hasn't worn it out of the house since the exchange shut, but he takes it down to show people.
# The hat moves on after Abel (world-layers pass, 2026-10-23; design/WORLD-LAYERS.md section 5). DRAFT, both states.
state: 3 stand | Abel's hat on the hall stand, where he left it the week he died. The brass band has gone dull. Mary dusts round it and won't move it, so Ned hangs his own on the newel post.
state: 4 bag | A paper bag on the high shelf with a hat's brim pushing it out. Nan gets it down for dressing up and Ruth tells her to put it back, and every time it goes back a bit nearer the edge.
in: 3 q3_furrowe_hall
in: 4 q4_furrowe_house

@prop q.brack_rifle
name: The rifle by the door
place: q_brack_kitchen
mark: rifle
tells: person q.will
macro: 2.4 2.2
carries: weight
touch: lift "Lift the rifle off the rack" | Heavier than it looks, and cold all through. The stock is smooth where Will's cheek goes. There's a little dent in the butt the size of a boy's heel. {sense: cold.iron}
state: 2 rack | Will's rifle on the rack by the door, unloaded. The rounds are in a tin on the top shelf. Davey has been up on a chair to look in it. He'll tell you if you ask.

# Tomas's cap (was the cell log; q.fact.cell_log and q.lore.cell_log mean the cap now, DEVICE-AUDIT 3.4)
@prop q.brack_nail
name: The nail behind the door
place: q_brack_kitchen
mark: rifle
tells: person q.tomas
carries: touch
touch: hold "Take the cap down" ? has(q.tomas_held) & cday() >= 45 | Brown wool, gone thin at the peak where a thumb pulled it down. It still has the shape of his head in it. It smells of the cells, and under that, of a boy. You hang it back on the nail the way it was. {sense: q.cap.hold, gives: q.lore.cell_log}
state: 2 cap ? has(q.tomas_held) & cday() >= 45 | Behind the door, on the nail over Will's coat, a boy's brown cap. Nobody in the house touches it. Edie dusts round it.
state: 2 coat | Will's greatcoat on the nail behind the door, still wet at the hem from the post road.

# The brazier at the post (was the district board). Its quoted state keeps the world record's last line, said by
# a constable at the fire, never written up: tests/worldrecord.test.mjs.
@prop q.post_board
name: The brazier at the post
place: q_post
mark: board
tells: era
carries: heat
touch: hold "Hold your hands over the brazier" | The heat comes up into your palms so fast it hurts, and your back stays as cold as it was. The constables stand round it so close their coats steam.
state: 2 quoted ? prior_runs >= 1 & prior_line != "" | The brazier at the post, and the constables round it. One of them says a thing over to himself the way you'd say a thing you'd heard in the Crown, and laughs, and says it again: "{{prior_line}}"
state: 2 brazier | The brazier at the post, a drum with holes punched in it, burning fence rails. The constables stand round it so close their coats steam. Somebody's child's drawing of a cart and a horse is burning on the top, curling up from the corners.

# Tesk's fold: the rock Ned's hand meets (q.lore.notebook, DEVICE-AUDIT 3.4)
@prop q.tesk_fold
name: The rock in Tesk's fold
place: q_hill
mark: fold
tells: person q.tesk
carries: touch
touch: press "Put your bare hand flat on the rock" ? era() == 2 | It bites. There's no seam in it, no slab, no give anywhere under the straw. It's the hill, all the way down. A goat comes and pushes her nose at your glove. {sense: q.rock.cold, gives: q.lore.notebook}
state: 2 bare | The fold with the straw kicked back, and the rock under it, grey, with frost in the cracks. The goats stand round it as if waiting to see what you'll do.

# The blue thread, felt (the thread rule: held, cut, tied; DEVICE-AUDIT 3.3)
@prop q.haldane_thread
name: The blue thread
place: q_haldane
mark: table
tells: person q.anni
carries: touch
touch: hold "Hold the thread" ? has(q.anni_sent) | It's soft as hair, and cold from the shelf. In one place it's flattened where Bet held it between her teeth all the way home from Tilney Road. {sense: thread.hold}
state: 2 shelf ? has(q.anni_sent) | Anni's blue thread on the shelf beside her bowl, in a loop, the way it came off her wrist.
state: 2 spool | The spare blue wool, wound on a peg on the shelf by the stove. Bet ties a new one on whoever's wears through. There's not much left on the peg.
